condition():\n        RETURN self.condition\n```\n', '|Case|:**track_quantity**\n```pseudocode\n// Tracking quantity is part of Equipment class\nFUNCTION get_quantity():\n    RETURN self.quantity\n```\n|Case|:**update_equipment**\n```pseudocode\nFUNCTION update_equipment(equipment):\n    FOR i, item IN enumerate(equipment_list):\n        IF item.name == equipment.name:\n            SET equipment_list[i] = equipment\n            CALL save_data()\n            BREAK\n```\n', '|Case|:**view_availability**\n```pseudocode\nFUNCTION get_availability():\n    RETURN self.availability\n```\n|Case|:**view_location**\n```pseudocode\nFUNCTION get_location():\n    RETURN self.location\n```\n', '|Case|:**set_alert**\n```pseudocode\nCLASS Alert:\n    FUNCTION __init__(name: str, alert_type: str):\n        SET self.name = name\n        SET self.alert_type = alert_type\n\nCLASS InventoryManager:\n    FUNCTION set_alert(name: str, alert_type: str):\n        CREATE new_alert = Alert(name, alert_type)\n        APPEND new_alert TO self.alerts\n        CALL save_alerts()\n```\n\n### Third-party Libraries:\n- **tkinter:** Used to create the graphical user interface (GUI) of the application, providing methods for creating windows, buttons, entry fields, checkboxes, etc.\n- **json:** Used for handling JSON data, serializing Python objects to JSON format when saving data, and deserializing JSON data to Python objects when loading data.']
